1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:01,960
Works with a mouse.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,800
But not with a keyboard.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,440
AI proposes a fix.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,320
Keyboard tasks: 0/2 → 2/2.

5
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,280
Accepted.

6
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:17,240
But readability got worse.

7
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,960
Contrast: 1.19:1.

8
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,400
Rejected.

9
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,920
Original preserved.

10
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,680
AccessFix independently verifies.

11
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,720
Fixes need proof.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,640
We built AccessFix AI
around a simple separation.

13
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,240
Meta Muse Spark proposes code.

14
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,800
An independent browser verifier
tests the outcome.

15
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,640
These are saved experiments on
project-authored test apps.

16
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,200
Both pointer tasks passed.

17
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,440
Both keyboard tasks failed.

18
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:52,200
ArrowRight left focus on Overview.

19
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,280
The saved patch adds navigation

20
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,160
and explicitly moves focus
to the selected tab.

21
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:01,160
Both keyboard tasks now pass.

22
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,680
Both pointer tasks still pass.

23
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:07,280
Checks also cover returning to Overview,

24
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:10,080
adding a note,
and persistence after reload.

25
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,200
Accepted on those measured checks.

26
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:16,600
The historical run was later
restored to the original.

27
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:21,360
The Switch candidate also passed
both keyboard tasks

28
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:23,600
and preserved both pointer tasks.

29
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,760
The patch used a native button.

30
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,440
It contained no CSS edit.

31
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:35,640
But the same Off label became harder to
read: 1.19:1, below 4.5:1.

32
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:40,760
That is a new confirmed
contrast violation.

33
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,760
AccessFix AI rejected the candidate.

34
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,960
The stored record selects the original
and confirms it stayed intact.

35
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:56,680
Inspect the actual model patch beside the
independent verification results.

36
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,200
Playwright checked completed tasks.

37
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:03,040
axe-core audited the observed states.

38
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:08,760
The final decision follows measured
outcomes, not the model's explanation.

39
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,120
Both experiments used
Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor,

40
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,280
one request each. No retry.

41
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,160
Menu still needs review.

42
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,440
Tic Tac Toe: new incomplete findings,
not violations.

43
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,320
Visual review found lost outlines.

44
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,840
AI generates the fix.

45
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,000
AccessFix AI proves whether it works.

46
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:39,000
Explore the read-only demo.

47
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:40,920
Inspect the evidence.
